Package: omx-plugins
Section: metapackages
Architecture: any
Depends: omx-plugins-clap (= ${binary:Version}), omx-plugins-lv2 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenMixer delay, drive, EQ, strip, gate and effects (CLAP, LV2)
 Take the sound of the OpenMixer console into your DAW or onto your own rig:
 delay, drive, the channel EQ as an 8-band EQ, a 16-band EQ or a 32-band EQ,
 a 31-band graphic EQ, the full channel strip and the keyed gate with its
 sidechain input, and the console's effects: chorus, flanger, phaser,
 tremolo, rotary speaker, reverb, pitch shifter, transient shaper, de-esser
 and limiter. They come as CLAP plugins for Bitwig, REAPER and Carla, and as
 LV2 plugins for Ardour, Carla, MOD and Zynthian. Each one runs the same DSP
 as the console, so a track sounds the same in a session as it does on the
 desk, sample for sample.
 .
 This package installs both formats; omx-plugins-clap and omx-plugins-lv2
 install one each.

Package: omx-plugins-clap
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenMixer delay, drive, EQ, strip, gate and effects as CLAP plugins
 The OpenMixer console's delay, drive, 8-, 16- and 32-band EQ, 31-band
 graphic EQ, channel strip, keyed gate and effects (chorus, flanger, phaser,
 tremolo, rotary speaker, reverb, pitch shifter, transient shaper, de-esser,
 limiter) as CLAP plugins, installed in /usr/lib/clap where Bitwig,
 REAPER, Carla and other CLAP hosts find them. They run the console's own DSP,
 so they sound like the desk, sample for sample.

Package: omx-plugins-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: all
Depends: libomxdsp-dev (>= 0.3.0), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Headers of the OpenMixer plugins, for projects that build on them
 The headers other projects include to use the OpenMixer plugins' parameters
 and instance code, such as omx_delay_instance.h and each plugin's generated
 parameter header, installed in /usr/include/omx-plugins.

Package: omx-plugins-lv2
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenMixer delay, drive, EQ, strip, gate and effects as LV2 plugins
 The OpenMixer console's delay, drive, 8-, 16- and 32-band EQ, 31-band
 graphic EQ, channel strip, keyed gate and effects (chorus, flanger, phaser,
 tremolo, rotary speaker, reverb, pitch shifter, transient shaper, de-esser,
 limiter) as LV2 plugins, installed in /usr/lib/lv2 where Ardour, Carla,
 MOD and Zynthian find them, with a MOD GUI where the plugin has one. They run
 the console's own DSP, so they sound like the desk, sample for sample.
